AWS Networking & Security Real-World Scenarios Interview Questions 🔐
#AWS #Security #VPC #IAM 
 
Let’s deep dive into how AWS handles security, identity, and networking — where one wrong config can expose your entire infra!

 These are real-world SRE & DevOps-level questions that test your design thinking, troubleshooting mindset 👇

Your EC2 instance can’t access the internet, but the route tables and IGW look fine — what could be wrong?
Your private subnet instances need to download updates from the internet — how would you enable it securely?
You deployed an application in multiple VPCs — how can you enable communication between them efficiently?
Your on-premise data center needs to connect securely to AWS — what are your connectivity options?
How do you protect your web application from SQL injection or DDoS attacks?
You found that some IAM users have overly permissive policies — how do you detect and remediate this?
Your Lambda function fails due to “AccessDenied” error — how do you troubleshoot IAM permissions for it?
How would you rotate IAM access keys automatically across all AWS accounts?
You need to allow access to an S3 bucket only from your company’s VPC — how do you configure that?
Your team wants to centralize security logs from all AWS accounts — which services and architecture would you use?
Your VPC CIDR is exhausted — how do you expand your IP range without downtime?
How can you securely expose an internal API to a third-party vendor?
You want to inspect and filter traffic at Layer 7 — which AWS service would you use and why?
How do you design a multi-region, low-latency network architecture using Route 53 and CloudFront?
Your application on EC2 can’t connect to an RDS database — what are the possible root causes?
How do you implement least-privilege access across a large AWS environment with hundreds of developers?
What’s the difference between Security Groups and NACLs, and when would you use each?
You need to enforce encryption in-transit and at-rest across all services ,how would you implement this in AWS?
How can you detect if an IAM role was assumed by an unauthorized user?
Your S3 bucket suddenly becomes public , how do you detect and prevent such misconfigurations in the future?
You need to implement central IAM governance for multiple AWS accounts , which AWS service can help?
How do you audit all configuration changes made in your AWS account automatically?
Your CloudFront distribution serves sensitive content , how do you secure it from unauthorized access?
How can you automate patching and compliance reporting for EC2 instances at scale?
